  "narrative": {
    "intro": "National Steel and Shipbuilding received $2.8B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. National Steel and Shipbuilding won 16 awards so far, with an average award size of $174M and obligations up 406.3% year over year. National Steel and Shipbuilding recorded obligations of $471M in FY21, $2.2B in FY22, $1.2B in FY23, $1.4B in FY24, $550M in FY25, and $2.8B in FY26. National Steel and Shipbuilding’s FY2026 totals are partial, covering the fiscal year to date. National Steel and Shipbuilding’s award count and average award size show that a small number of large awards drive the current-year total. The FY26 jump follows a lower base year in FY25 of $550M and recent year-to-year swings, including the $2.2B in FY22. National Steel and Shipbuilding’s profile for FY2026 to date reflects concentrated, high-dollar obligations rather than many small contracts. This overview summarizes obligational scale, award concentration, and the recent fiscal-year sequence of obligations.",
